BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Beginner Knitting Course - January
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20270110T123000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20270110T140000
UID:bistitchual-10520211751170@bistitchual.ca
DESCRIPTION:This listing is for a three session Beginner Knitting Course. 
 The classes will be held in person at Bistitchual on Sunday January 10th\,
  17th and 24th from 12:30-2:00pm Have you always wanted to learn to knit? 
 We’ve got you covered! Beginner Knitting is a course for brand new begin
 ners\, and over these three 1.5hr classes\, Anna will teach you everything
  you need to create a basic project from beginning to end. Our class size 
 is capped at 4 people\, so everyone can receive the attention they need. A
 nna will share lots of tips and techniques to get you well on your way. (N
 o experience necessary) Materials: Yarn and needles will be provided. What
  We’ll Learn - How to make a slip knot. - Casting on. - The Knit stitch.
  - The Purl stitch. - Exploring Knit / Purl combinations. - Binding off. -
  Weaving in ends. - Fixing common mistakes and how to avoid them. - Common
  uses of flat knitting. - Intro into Ravelry. Please note that classes wil
 l only proceed if we have a minimum of two attendees . If the minimum is n
 ot met\, there will be the option for a refund or to reschedule. There wil
 l be a four person maximum for each class. Please pre-book your spot to le
 t us know you are coming! About the instructor: If idle hands are the Devi
 l’s tools\, he hasn’t much to do with Anna (she/they.) Anna’s grandm
 other taught her to knit as a toddler and she hasn’t put the yarn down s
 ince. Knitting\, crochet\, spinning\, dyeing\, embroidery\, hand sewing\, 
 machine sewing - Anna has a voracious appetite for learning new textile te
 chniques. With a background in textile artifact conservation\, Anna explor
 es the craft\, history\, and science behind fibre arts. Cancellation Polic
 y Classes must be paid for at the time of registration to reserve your spo
 t. - If cancelled 48 hrs or more prior to the start of the first class wil
 l be given a store credit. Classes cancelled less than 48 hrs prior to the
  start of the class will not be reimbursed.
LOCATION:Bistitchual\, 266 Jane St\, Toronto\, ON M6S 3Z2
URL:https://bistitchual.ca/products/beginner-knitting-course-january-1
X-SOURCE:Bistitchual
END:VEVENT
